    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85765" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόρ-ισμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, Geom., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>deduction from a previous demonstration,
			corollary,</i> as it were a <i>windfall</i> or <i>bonus</i>
			(cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορίζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.2
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				3.1
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Alc.</u>
				p.139C.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>in CA</u>
				23p.469M.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				251
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορίζω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			) <i>a kind of proposition intermediate between a theorem and
				a problem,</i> defined by <i><span class="en">
				Papp.
				648.18
			</span></i> sqq., <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>in Euc.</u>
				p.301F.
			</span></i></div>
